cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Anvaya, please cite both the software and the paper below."
title: "Anvaya: a toolkit for parsimony analysis of chromosome fusion-and-mixing characters"
abstract: >-
  Anvaya turns chromosome-scale synteny data into a parsimony-based
  phylogenetic hypothesis. It builds reciprocal-best-hit orthology with
  DIAMOND, defines ancestral linkage groups from either a single reference
  genome or a multi-genome consensus, scores ancestral-linkage-group fusion
  and post-fusion mixing as discrete irreversible characters, and reconstructs
  trees under both reversible and Camin-Sokal criteria with bootstrap,
  permutation and consistency-index support. It additionally detects and
  rescues ohnologs from whole-genome duplications, which plain reciprocal best
  hit otherwise discards.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/REPLACE-ME/anvaya"
url: "https://github.com/REPLACE-ME/anvaya"
keywords:
  - macrosynteny
  - ancestral linkage groups
  - parsimony
  - phylogenomics
  - chromosome evolution
  - whole-genome duplication
  - comparative genomics
authors:
  - family-names: Kulkarni
    given-names: Siddharth S.
    affiliation: "CSIR-Centre for Cellular and Molecular Biology, Hyderabad, India"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/REPLACE-ME"
